## 3. Drift found

None. Every paper header matches the boards' honest state. The moonshots that the boards call residual, the papers also call theoretical. The shipped features the boards call done, the papers also describe as design. The CONFLICTS.oot matrix is the only place where draft papers collide with product claims, and that collision is named and prioritized.

## 4. Recommended promotion

None yet. The 49 papers should stay `draft` until a human reads them. The P0 conflicts in CONFLICTS.oot (C4, C7, C8, C9) already reflect the boards' honest view, so the conflict synthesis is ahead of the per-paper review. If you want to start promotion, the four P0 conflicts are the natural first batch.

## 5. What this audit did not check

- Paper body (H2+) for factual accuracy against code.
- Cross-paper consistency (whether RP-3-7's ARC story matches RP-6-2's tension resolution).
- Whether each paper's section 7 (product reality) matches SHIPPED today.

A second pass could check the paper bodies section by section. This pass only confirmed the headers align.
